  "prompt": "# Adversarial review: Block/Ignore Users \u2014 firmware half (Offband, #241)\n\nYou are an adversarial firmware reviewer for Offband (a MeshCore fork; C++17, ESP32 + nRF52, PlatformIO). Review the consolidated diff (vs `firmware-base`) for **real correctness/safety/security/interop defects only** \u2014 severity BLOCKER / MAJOR / MINOR, each with file:line and a concrete fix. Skip style/naming nits.\n\n## What this change does\nAdds the Offband-only **firmware half** of user blocking: a portable, node-resident pubkey block list on the **companion** that drops blocked DMs at the device and syncs to/from the phone app over the companion-API link. **Receive-side only** \u2014 by design it must NOT change forwarding, relaying, adverts, channels, or any RF/mesh path (interop with stock MeshCore repeaters must be preserved). Adverts/channel-name blocking are handled app-side, out of firmware scope.\n\nComponents in the diff:\n1. **`src/helpers/BlockStore.h`** \u2014 pure, dependency-free (only `<cstdint>`/`<cstring>`), fixed-capacity set of 32 \u00d7 32-byte pubkeys: `add` (dedup, capacity-bounded), `remove` (swap-remove), `contains`, `count`, `keyAt` (bounds-checked, returns nullptr OOB), `clear`. Native-unit-tested (3 googletest cases, included in diff).\n2. **`OffbandConfigProtocol.h`** \u2014 `OFFBAND_CAP_BLOCK=0x02` cap bit; `CMD_OFFBAND_BLOCK=0xC2` + sub-codes `ADD=0x01/REMOVE=0x02/LIST=0x03/CLEAR=0x04` (companion-API 0xC0+ fork space; never on the mesh).\n3. **`MyMesh.h/.cpp`**:\n   - `FIRMWARE_VER_CODE` 14\u219215; sets `OFFBAND_CAP_BLOCK` unconditionally in the `CMD_DEVICE_QUERY` caps byte. The `OffbandConfigProtocol.h` include was hoisted out of `#ifdef OFFBAND_OBSERVER` so the `offband` namespace resolves on every companion build (header is self-contained: only `<stdint.h>`, constants+enums).\n   - `BlockStore _blocks;` member. **The only enforcement point**: an early `if (_blocks.contains(from.id.pub_key)) return;` at the top of `queueMessage` (the app-push layer, after routing). Claim: the mesh ACK is emitted by the routing layer *before* the `onMessageRecv`\u2192`queueMessage` callback, so this early-return does not suppress ACKs or change RF behavior. **Verify that claim against the diff/your knowledge of MeshCore.**\n   - Persistence: flat `/blocks` file `[count:1][key:32]*count`, loaded at boot after `loadContacts`, saved on change. The blob API (`putBlobByKey`) was rejected because its length arg is `uint8_t` (\u2264255 B) and the list is up to 1+32*32=1025 B. Added `DataStore::openWriteFile()` (thin wrapper over the file-local static `openWrite()` so the per-platform open-flag ladder isn't duplicated; named *openWriteFile* to avoid C++ member-name-hiding the static used by savePrefs/saveContacts/saveChannels).\n   - **0xC2 handler**: ADD/REMOVE persist + single-frame ack `[0xC2][sub][ok]`; CLEAR acks; unknown sub \u2192 `ERR_CODE_ILLEGAL_ARG`. **LIST is streamed** (not synchronous): verified `SerialBLEInterface::writeFrame` *drops* (returns 0) when the send queue is full (depth 12 BLE / 4 WiFi), so a synchronous \u226434-frame LIST would silently drop keys. So LIST writes a START frame `[0xC2][LIST][0xFF][count]`, sets `_blk_listing`, and `blockListDrain()` emits one key frame `[0xC2][LIST][idx][32B key]` per idle main-loop pass (gated `!isWriteBusy()`), then END `[0xC2][LIST][0xFE]`. `idx` is 0..31 so it never collides with 0xFF/0xFE. The index is re-checked against live `count()` each pass.\n\n## Focus questions\n1. **Interop (\u00a711):** does anything here change forwarding/relay/advert/channel/RF behavior? Is the \"ACK is on the routing layer, before queueMessage\" claim correct \u2014 i.e. is the early-return in `queueMessage` truly app-push-only?\n2. **`queueMessage` drop:** `from.id.pub_key` is the right field and 32 bytes? Any caller of `queueMessage` where an early return leaks a packet/buffer or skips required cleanup (e.g. `pkt` release)? Does dropping there skip anything other than app notification (offline-queue, UI, contact-sync persistence)?\n3. **Persistence:** `/blocks` read/write correctness across nRF52 (`FILE_O_WRITE`/`FILE_O_READ`), RP2040 (`\"w\"/\"r\"`), ESP32 (`\"w\",true`/`\"r\",false`). Truncation on rewrite? Partial-read / corrupt-file handling (`f.read` short read)? Boot-load bounded to `MAX_BLOCKED_KEYS`?\n4. **0xC2 handler:** frame-length validation (`len >= 2`, `len >= 2+PUB_KEY_SIZE`), `out_frame` overflow (MAX_FRAME_SIZE=176; key frame=35 B), any path that writes a malformed/over-length frame.\n5. **LIST streaming state machine:** can `_blk_listing` get stuck set (never reaches END)? Re-entrancy if a second LIST arrives mid-stream? A concurrent ADD/REMOVE/CLEAR mid-stream \u2014 can it cause a read past the array, a dup, or a skipped key (and is that acceptable)? Interaction/precedence with the observer config stream (`_ob_stream`) and the contacts iterator (`_iter_started`) in the same `else if` chain.\n6. **BlockStore:** any off-by-one in capacity/dedup/swap-remove; `keyAt` OOB; `memcmp`/`memcpy` sizing.\n7. **Caps byte / version gate:** is bumping `FIRMWARE_VER_CODE` 14\u219215 and adding the cap bit additive/back-compatible for pre-v15 clients (they read a shorter frame / ignore the bit)?\n\n## Diff (vs firmware-base)\n=== C:\\Users\\stryc\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Dev-meshcore-firmware\\82e07da7-e795-4b7b-a548-defa53fba619\\scratchpad\\block-consol.diff ===\ndiff --git a/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp b/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp\nindex bf2f36c3..e9534f55 100644\n--- a/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp\n+++ b/examples/companion_radio/DataStore.cpp\n@@ -155,6 +155,14 @@ File DataStore::openRead(FILESYSTEM* fs, const char* filename) {\n #endif\n }\n \n+// #241: truncating write-open on the primary FS, via the file-local openWrite()\n+// helper so the per-platform flags live in exactly one place. Named openWriteFile\n+// (not openWrite) so it does not hide the file-local static openWrite() tha